In short: moleculo is free for academic, non-profit and personal non-commercial
use. A company may evaluate it free for 30 days; any other commercial use needs
a paid commercial licence. The definitions below decide which case applies.

1. DEFINITIONS

   "Academic Use" means use by a student, teacher or researcher of an
   accredited university, college or other degree-granting educational
   institution, for teaching, study or research whose results the institution
   is free to publish without delay or restriction.

   "Non-Profit Use" means use by a registered charity or other
   non-governmental non-profit organisation for its own non-commercial
   research or educational purposes.

   "Personal Use" means use by an individual for their own purposes, outside
   any paid work and not on behalf of any organisation.

   "Commercial Use" means any use that is not Academic, Non-Profit or Personal
   Use. Any use described in (a) to (d) below is Commercial Use even where it
   would otherwise meet one of those definitions. It includes, without
   limitation:
   a. any use by or on behalf of a for-profit company, including its internal
      research and development;
   b. research carried out under contract for, or funded by, a for-profit
      company where that company receives the results or rights in them
      ahead of publication, or exclusively;
   c. providing services to others for a fee — such as contract research,
      screening, or library and compound searching — using the software;
   d. using the software in or alongside a product or service that is sold.

   "Evaluation" means Commercial Use solely to assess whether to obtain a
   commercial licence, on non-production systems, without using the results
   in any commercial decision or deliverable.

